TEXT -224 -736 Left 6 ;This example shows that the additional line is the best solution to increase the voltage niveau\n, hold the voltage in the linear domain and to make the voltageshape more flat\nq7-load is sweeped from -0.3 till +0.376\nThe voltage in Bus7 is now stabilized
TEXT 1152 0 Left 5 ;To stabilize the voltage at node 7 you can:\n \n1)  Insert a new line e.g. from node 2 to node 7 to make the impedance of the \n     network smaller\n     This example is named Emtex_result.asc\n \n2)  Compensate the node with a capacitor-battery at node 7\n     This example is named Emtex_result_2.asc\n \n3) Insert voltage controlled nodes (pv-nodes) at node 3 and 5\n    This examples are named: \n     Emtex_pvslack_result_3.asc (.op analysis ) and\n     Emtex_pvslack_result_3_tran.asc ( .trans analysis ) and\n     Emtex_pvslack_t_result_3.asc (.tran analysis and with transient pv-slack model )\n \n4) Stabilize the voltage by changing the voltage\n    translation factor of all three transformers to \n    l_=-3 or time varying ( higher secondary voltage )\n   This example is named Emtex_result_4.asc (.OP analysis )\n   and Emtex_result_4_tran.asc ( .TRAN analysis with timevarying tranformer taping )
TEXT 760 -96 Left 5 ;New line
TEXT -400 -56 Left 5 ;NOTE: All values (voltages,currents,powers) are normalized\n            in this example
TEXT -304 -368 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}
